<title>USA: American Greetings in unit sales, buyback.</title>
<headline>American Greetings in unit sales, buyback.</headline>
<dateline>CLEVELAND 1997-06-19</dateline>
<text>
<p>American Greetings Corp said Thursday it agreed to sell two subsidiaries, Acme Frame Products and Wilhold, to Newell Co and simultaneously announced a share repurchase program.</p>
<p>The company said it plans to buy back up to 4.5 million shares of its stock, or about six percent of the current 75.2 million shares outstanding, on the open market. It did not set a timeframe for the buy backs.</p>
<p>American Greetings said the spin-off of its two subsidiaries would generate a one-time pre-tax gain of about $22 million ($14 million after taxes) or $0.18 per share.</p>
</text>
